    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8",
    "original_text": "Exact bounded statement:\nFinite real Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; any function F:E->R, any translation p:E and a real scale s!=0.\nNo continuity, measurability of F, exponential integrability, probability or moment premise. Equality is of Mathlib totalized normalized tilted measures; probability is a separate obligation for every consumer.\nThe actual pushforward of the normalized Lebesgue Gibbs tilt under x->p+s*x is the normalized Lebesgue tilt with inverse-affine potential x->F(s^-1*(x-p)). The nonzero actual Lebesgue Jacobian cancels between partition and set numerator. This canonical identity alone makes no probability assertion.\nSource realκ>=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0<eta<=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta<=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.",
    "text_sha256": "25a02eaf3fcf4259baf20eac1ecb5d87499d4bb56ed514dab97c97c4d6fb8829"
